# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artifacts of the end-to-end suite. NONE of these belongs in version control.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS HERE AND NOT AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT
# The refactor plan records that no change to the root `.gitignore` is required, and that file is
# therefore left exactly as the legacy repository has it. `tests/e2e/` is a directory this refactor
# creates, so the ignore rules for what it generates belong inside it. A nested `.gitignore` applies
# to its own directory and everything beneath it, which is precisely the scope wanted: these rules
# must not accidentally suppress a same-named path elsewhere in the tree.
#
# The root file also already carries a pre-existing inconsistency - it excludes /pack/* while pack/
# is tracked - which sits inside the read-only region and is not this suite's to resolve. Adding
# Node-specific rules there would edit a file the migration treats as out of bounds, to solve a
# problem that exists only in this directory.
#
# WHY IT IS NOT MERELY TIDINESS
# `npm ci` materializes several hundred megabytes under `node_modules/`, and a Playwright run writes
# report and trace directories. Without these rules a routine `git add -A` commits all of it. Traces
# and reports are the more serious of the two: a trace records request and response bodies, so a run
# against a configured environment can capture a bearer token or other credential material verbatim.
# Keeping them untracked is a secrets control, not housekeeping.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED
# `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `playwright.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `fixtures/` and
# `specs/` are all committed. The lock file in particular must be tracked: `npm ci` requires it and
# fails without it, and it is what makes an install reproducible.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Installed dependencies
node_modules/

# Playwright run output: results, HTML report, and the sharded/merged report formats
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# TypeScript incremental build state, emitted next to tsconfig.json by --incremental/--build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment overrides. Never commit a populated environment file: the base URLs are harmless
# but the client-certificate and token settings this suite reads are not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The ephemeral mutual-TLS client identity written by `npm run provision:identity`: a throwaway
# certificate authority and a client leaf whose common name is the identity the suite claims. This
# directory holds PRIVATE KEYS, so the rule is a secrets control rather than housekeeping - and it is the
# reason the script may write here at all. Fresh material is generated on every run and is never shared
# between environments, so there is nothing here worth keeping and everything here worth not committing.
# The repository's own secrets inventory exists because committed key material is the defect this
# refactor is remediating; do not add an exception to this rule.
.mtls/
